WEBVTT

00:00:00.970 --> 00:00:04.301
Routed value vectors, and a KV cache that doesn't notice.

00:00:04.301 --> 00:00:07.300
The mixture is summed before the cache is written.

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:12.869
The claim, from IFM's model card: No additional KV cache cost

00:00:12.869 --> 00:00:14.531
compared to standard GQA.

00:00:14.531 --> 00:00:15.361
It holds.

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:20.063
MoVA against a plain GQA v_proj.

00:00:20.063 --> 00:00:21.317
Weights: 64×.

00:00:21.317 --> 00:00:23.199
Decode FLOPs: 4×.

00:00:23.199 --> 00:00:25.080
KV cache: 1×.

00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:37.350
20.2% of the entire model sits in the value experts: 7,549,747,200 parameters.

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:42.757
Collapse the mixture before the cache, and everything downstream stays ordinary.

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:50.108
